    "en": {
      "title": "EXM 701",
      "h1": "weber EXM 701",
      "description": "weber EXM 701 is an expanding concrete that is mixed with water only into an expanding mass, specially intended for thin grouting (5-50 mm).",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "image",
          "alt": "weber logotyp",
          "href": "/produkter/weber",
          "width": 880,
          "height": 262,
          "src": "/assets/img/weber-logo.webp",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "alt": "weber EXM 701",
          "src": "/assets/img/weber-exm-701-main.webp",
          "width": 735,
          "height": 1048,
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "weber EXM 701 is an expanding concrete that is mixed with water only into an expanding mass, specially intended for thin grouting (5-50 mm). It normally gives good adhesion to adjoining surfaces and good corrosion protection for embedded parts of untreated steel. Compressive strength above 50 MPa.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Grouting under and around parts, especially thin layers (5-50 mm)",
            "Very good adhesion to steel",
            "Meets the requirements for grouting mortars according to AMA Anläggning",
            "CE marked to EN 1504-6",
            "Registered in BASTA, rated Accepted in Byggvarubedömningen"
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "stat",
          "label": "Consumption",
          "value": "approx. 2 kg/l",
          "unit": "of mixed mortar",
          "meta": "thin layers, 5-50 mm",
          "note": "Yield approx. 10 litres per 20 kg bag with 3.6 litres of water.",
          "usage": true,
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "kind": "download",
          "text": "Technical data sheet (TDS)",
          "href": "/assets/docs/weber-exm-701-tekniskt-datablad.pdf",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "kind": "download",
          "text": "Safety data sheet (SDS)",
          "href": "/assets/docs/weber-exm-701-sakerhetsdatablad.pdf",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "kind": "download",
          "text": "Declaration of performance (DoP)",
          "href": "/assets/docs/weber-exm-701-prestandadeklaration.pdf",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "kind": "download",
          "text": "Environmental product declaration (EPD)",
          "href": "/assets/docs/weber-exm-701-epd.pdf",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Areas of use",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Grouting under steel and concrete columns, bridge bearings and concrete elements",
            "Casting in of bolts, railing posts and columns in column sleeves",
            "Layers up to 50 mm where all sides of the casting space are fixed and complete filling is required",
            "Horizontal concrete repairs and injection work. Anchoring: hole diameter matched to the bar (e.g. Ø 16 mm bar in a Ø 30 mm hole), anchoring length at least 150 mm"
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "text": "Limitations",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Do not use when the temperature may fall below +5 °C",
            "Embedded parts of untreated aluminium must not be used; galvanised parts are protectively painted where they are cast in"
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
